  "title": "Reconcile kiokoto branch with main after module rename",
  "start_head": "0bf5f715cb1258bd277dad7269e1f74a508499cc",
  "preexisting_changes": {},
  "spec": {
    "problem": "PR #4 (kiokoto -> main) fails CI: GitHub tests the merge of kiokoto into current main (7ee92f8a). After the branch point, main gained FLASH-431, whose Go files import the pre-rename module path github.com/kotobawork/nihongo-bjt/api-go/... while BRAND-414 renamed the module to github.com/kiokoto/nihongo-bjt/api-go, so the merged tree does not build (go-checks) and the lifecycle check flags the merge-touched files whose content no closed task verified.",
    "acceptance": [
      {
        "id": "AC1",
        "text": "origin/main (7ee92f8a, FLASH-431) is merged into kiokoto with no unresolved conflicts; FLASH-431 content is preserved intact except for Go module import paths"
      },
      {
        "id": "AC2",
        "text": "No .go file in the merged tree references the old module path github.com/kotobawork/nihongo-bjt (grep count 0); the four FLASH-431 httpserver handler files import github.com/kiokoto/nihongo-bjt/api-go/...; go build ./... passes"
      },
      {
        "id": "AC3",
        "text": "bash scripts/quality/verify-go.sh passes on the merged tree against the canonical test schema (including the FLASH-431 deck_moderation migration), and the CI lifecycle check (cli.mjs check --ci --base origin/main --head HEAD) reports no UNOWNED or STALE files for the PR range"
      },
      {
        "id": "AC4",
        "text": "No behavior change beyond merge + import reconciliation: merged flashcarddeck/store.go, httpserver/server.go and admin messages equal the union of both parents; route-contract check (go run ./cmd/route-contract -check) passes without regenerating docs/openapi.json or docs/api-route-inventory.json"
      }
    ],
    "expected_behavior": "",
    "observed_behavior": "",
    "rollback_plan": "Revert the merge commit and the import-fix commit on kiokoto (git revert -m 1 <merge> + git revert <fix>); the branch returns to 0bf5f715 (BRAND-413) and main is never touched. The FLASH-431 deck_moderation migration is additive (new tables only, owned by FLASH-431 on main) and is not altered by this task, so no database rollback is required; if the branch were ever deployed merged (it is not - PR is draft, deploy runs from main), rollback is the same revert plus redeploy of the previous main SHA."
  },
